[Event "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[StudyName "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[ChapterName "Classical: 4...Bf5"]
[Orientation "black"]

1. e4 c6 {The Caro-Kann: Black prepares ...d5 with a pawn supporting it, and keeps a rock-solid structure.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 {Develops the bishop outside the pawn chain before playing ...e6.} 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 {White's sharpest try: threatens h5 to trap the bishop.} h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bf4 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 13. Kb1 {White has more space, Black has no weaknesses.}

[Event "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[StudyName "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[ChapterName "Advance Variation: 3.e5"]
[Orientation "black"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {White gains space.} Bf5 {The point of the Caro-Kann: the bishop gets out before ...e6.} 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 c5 {Strike at the centre at once.} 6. Be3 cxd4 7. Nxd4 Ne7

[Event "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[StudyName "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[ChapterName "Exchange Variation: 3.exd5"]
[Orientation "black"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 {The Panov Attack: White fights for the centre.} Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Nf3 Be7 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Bd3 Nc6 9. O-O O-O {An isolated queen's pawn position: play actively with the pieces.}
